        "original_id": "7811ceb7-b468-586b-a08a-47f601b079b5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Michael Kanin, Ring Lardner Jr.\n- Roles: director, producer, playwright, screenwriter, journalist\n- Awards: Academy Award\n- Films: Woman of the Year\n- Topics: Hollywood blacklist, Red Scare\n\nFacts:\n- Michael Kanin was born on February 1, 1910, and he died on March 12, 1993.\n- Ring Lardner Jr. was born on August 19, 1915, and he died on October 31, 2000.\n- Michael Kanin was an American director, producer, playwright, and screenwriter.\n- In 1942, Michael Kanin shared an Academy Award with Ring Lardner Jr. for writing the Katharine Hepburn-Spencer Tracy film comedy \"Woman of the Year.\"\n- Ring Lardner Jr. was an American journalist and screenwriter.\n- Ring Lardner Jr. was blacklisted by Hollywood movie studios during the Red Scare of the late 1940s and 1950s.",
